# The session font, parsed and rasterized in RING 3.
#
# A .ttf is attacker-shaped data and this is where it is parsed, so a
# malformed font crashes a restartable service instead of the kernel --
# the split Windows made when it moved font parsing to fontdrvhost.
#
# NO Target=, so it runs in `text` as well as `graphical`: the GUI
# Terminal and every windowed app want the session face, and a machine
# that starts a desktop by hand later should already have one published.
#
# Ready=notify, so a service ordered after this one waits for the atlas
# to actually exist. It notifies even when it published NOTHING (a
# `builtin` face, or a missing file): the desktop works on the baked
# tables either way, and refusing to come up would take the session down
# over a cosmetic problem.
#
# See docs/commands/fontd.md.
Name=fontd
Description=Rasterize the session font for every client
Exec=/bin/fontd
Restart=always
Ready=notify
